    "sha256": "aeddece11bb6f60454b621d82cbb5b4246c92acb94010cb7e451f07d6951b9e7"
  },
  "declaration_lines": {
    "closeS": 37,
    "eqS": 41,
    "memS": 44,
    "domS": 47,
    "intF": 61,
    "eval_closeS": 77,
    "eval_eqS": 81,
    "eval_memS": 90,
    "eval_domS": 110,
    "eval_intF": 197,
    "PN": 271,
    "shift_quote_sen": 273,
    "isSemiformula_quote_sen": 278,
    "good_PN": 289,
    "quote_intF": 321
  },
  "scope": [
    "closeS rewrites every free variable to the newest bound slot. The three selected formulas are closed semisentences of arities 2/2/1. Closed here means no free variable; these still have displayed bound slots.",
    "eval_eqS/eval_memS/eval_domS identify the native quotient meanings. Semantics assumes Nonempty M, SetStructure M and M models NativeSet.nativeTheory. The well-founded predicate is the repository internal represented-set minimal-element property, not external well-foundedness over arbitrary subsets.",
    "eval_intF is an external metatheoretic structural recursion on ordinary finite Foundation syntax. Its environment consists of native-domain elements, sent by cls to the quotient well-founded part. Quantifier directions use actual quotient representatives; no quotient-invariance hypothesis has been silently substituted for surjectivity.",
    "good_PN is uniform in every arithmetic IΣ1 model W, with arbitrary internal relation selector R. Its three formula codes are quotations of fixed standard semisentences; no native model or interpreted-axiom derivability premise is needed for this syntactic Good result.",
    "quote_intF is uniform over arithmetic models W but its input formula and binder arity are metatheoretic φ : SetTheorySemiproposition n and n : Nat. It identifies standard quoted formulas; it is not uniform transport of arbitrary internal/nonstandard formula codes.",
    "No theorem here supplies native Provable exists-domain, interpreted equality/fixed axioms, or the hAx callback for arbitrary internal ZF axiom codes, including nonstandard Separation and Replacement. Those and R2 remain open."
  ],
  "minimal_extraction": [
    "Extract closeS plus shift_quote_sen/isSemiformula_quote_sen first. Their proof bodies need syntax quotation and rewriting, not NativeTheory semantics or WFModel. The separately drafted RawFormQuotation does exactly this with a local exact copy of Translation.toSet/variable splitting.",
    "Then select the same three raw formulas, close them explicitly and quote them; the generic semisentence helpers directly give Good without evaluating large freeMax bounds. Import the newly checked reduced InternalInterpretation plus only the actual raw-form providers needed.",
    "The previous NativeWFParameters draft instead quotes unclosed toSet formulas. PN cannot be silently identified with that parameter: prove emb(closeS(toSet k raw)) = toSet k raw using no-free-variable support, or consistently adopt closed PN with its own semantic lemmas. This source review does not assert such a code equality.",
    "To extract quote_intF later, additionally isolate or reuse ConstructibleInterpretation.isUFormula_quote and quote_neg_set and the generic substitution prefix lemma. Avoid importing the complete NativeTheory dependency route solely to obtain these syntax lemmas."
  ],
  "frontier_delta": "Upstream ac89f2e948 supplies fixed closed WF-quotient interpretation formulas, a Good parameter in every IΣ1 model, an external semantic equivalence through the quotient class map, and a standard-formula quotation bridge. Reviewed here from source only. Native domain nonemptiness and uniform interpreted-axiom proofs, especially nonstandard Separation/Replacement matrices, remain required before the generic checked interpretation core closes R3. The binary/arithmetic interpreter comparison and R2 are separate.",
  "evidence_limits": [
    "The broad NativeTheory/WFModel/ConstructibleInterpretation import route was read for API dependencies but was not freshly built or audited here.",
    "The fresh core run validates only the narrowed InternalInterpretation module; it is not evidence of a fresh NativeInterp build."
  ],
  "related_sources": [
